:: Carter Connor Part 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 30>>
The two of you arrive at the Opal City cemetery about 20 minutes later, the walk there mostly filled with a nervous <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> wondering how much trouble you’ll get in for being late and coming here without permission. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Think my parents will be mad? I know it’s normal to want to come to a place like this but… do you think I should have asked for permission first? May- maybe we should go back…”</span> You reassure <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> that if this is what he wants to do, he should do it. <span style="Color: Yellow">He doesn’t need permission to visit his brother’s grave.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah… yeah, you’re right…”</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

It takes you both a few minutes to even find where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s grave is, since he’s only been here once and there isn’t really a map. Morbidly, there is a section of the cemetery for those who died young and, after some searching, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> stops suddenly in front of a small grave. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This is it.”</span> He pauses, <span style="Color: Yellow">looking a little stunned to actually be standing here.</span> You walk next to him and put your hand on his shoulder as he reads the plaque. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Here lies <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> Kent. Beloved brother and son. Gone, but not forgotten.”</span> There is a long pause as he looks it over as if he wants to see every little detail, to make sure it’s real. You look over it as well, staring at the inscription. <span style="Color: Yellow"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> was only a little over 3 when he died. It’s hard to believe someone so young passed. He didn’t even get to live his life yet.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> steps in front of the grave and sits down on the grass, legs crossed as he just stares up at it. He chuckles as he points to a small carving in the corner of the gravestone. You instantly recognize it as the Owlman symbol and ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> why it’s on his brother’s gravestone. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We both loved superheroes. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> said once that the best way to get us to stop crying when we were still babies was to put us in front of Hero Friends. You know, that old superhero cartoon? The bright colors and music still feel nostalgic for me. That Ultraman bear I have; they came in a set. I got all the Ultraman stuff, since I was quiet and gentle and would sleep through the night. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> was Owlman, since he always seemed active at night, causing trouble.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> laughs, <span style="Color: LightGreen">smiling as he stares down at the little symbol, rubbing it with his hands.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t actually know if that was his favorite hero, but I hope so, since Ultraman and Owlman are best friends.”</span> <br>
<br>
You sit down next to him, mentioning that your own little brother Noah is obsessed with Owlman. He seems pretty popular, so you’d bet it would have been his favorite. Though you doubt his collection would have been as crazy as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s. <span style="Color: Pink">He laughs at this, agreeing with you.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s weird, being here.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> leans back in the grass, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ve… always been so scared to come here alone and never wanted to bother my family with it. But – I don’t know – now that I’m here, I don’t know why I was so scared. I guess it makes it real, but…”</span> He takes a deep breath, just staring at the small limestone block. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Do you think I would have remembered his face, if we didn’t look the same? I was so little, I hardly remember anything about him. And even what I do remember… it’s so blurry, like a dream. Maybe… maybe what I’m remembering was a dream?”</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Ask him what he remembers">>
    You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> what he remembers and he thinks for a moment. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We’re… in our room. We shared a room the entire time he was alive, though my parents always planned to have 3 kids so… they had the extra room for when we got older. But I remember being sleepy, but I couldn’t get in our bed, since it had these little gates to stop us from rolling out of it. I was whining a lot, guess I was really tired.”</span> He laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We had this small cot in the closet that dad used to sleep on. He slept in our room a lot, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> too. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> never really slept well, cried a lot, so they’d have to calm him down a few times almost every night.”</span> He pauses there for a moment, thinking about these memories and details. <span style="Color: Yellow">He hadn’t thought about them for a long time.</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                    Blush: 1,
                    Cry: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I was so sleepy but I didn’t want to sleep on the floor. I don’t know why, maybe I was just stubborn. Heh… So, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> thought we should get the cot that they used. It was in the closet, standing up. It wasn’t that big, and was pretty light, but we still had to work together to get it down. Though, once we did, I was wide awake and energized from moving it. So, we just… put it back.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles nervously and rubs the back of his head, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Kinda weird, I know. But… it’s the main memory I think about whenever I remember him. It’s… blurry. Really blurry, but… I remember the cot was bright blue. I wonder if we still have it somewhere.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightGreen">You sit with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> for a long time, just listening to him talk about his brother. He rambles a bit, but he just looks so happy. To talk about his brother, his real brother. Not the shadow that his mom sees that has lingered in the house since he died. He talks about little pictures he’s seen or stories <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> told him. All the stories and details are so simple, stuff anyone could do any day of the week. But the way he talks about them, they feel special.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I dream about him a lot.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and you are now lying in the grass next to the grave, just talking as time drifts away. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sometimes we are heroes, stopping evil and stuff. But a lot of the time we just… talk? I don’t know, it’s kinda silly. Maybe it makes me a little crazy like me mom but… those are my favorite dreams. I know it’s not really him, but it’s nice. I told him about you, after that time at the park. I think, if you ever did meet him, he would have liked you.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    [[Continue|Carter Connor Part 3]]
<</linkreplace>>